Minimal pair vs the now-working direct spelling: expanding
`__enable_if_t<_Bn::value>...` (an alias template with a defaulted
second parameter, [temp.alias]) in __and_fn's trailing return breaks
the constrained-constructor deduction; spelling the same expansion as
`typename enable_if<_Bn::value, void>::type...` works.  Residual
layer of cpp17_optional_requires_ctor_pair (libstdc++ _Requires /
std::optional).  g++/clang++/valgrind run clean.
